> Keep in mind "Abundance ~ study site" means that *lambda* is different for each study site. I imagine that estimates of the latent N's for the cameras within each study site might look more like you were expecting. How you want to summarize this is up to you--a Bayesian approach may or may not make it easier to derive uncertainty intervals around the average/summed/etc realized abundance. What this derived thing actually means is unclear, but I imagine it correlates with the actual density of wallabies to some extent.
