Hello,

Thanks for the great R library!

I am working with repeated count distance sampling data from a rock iguana survey and have been able to set up everything for my site level and site - repeat level (yearlysitecovs) covariates but I also have site-repeat-observation level covariates that I would like to model but not sure if it is possible using the 'unmarkedframeGDS' and 'gdistsamp' functions? I have observation level covariates such as animal behaviour, age class, and detection mode that are likely to affect the detection process. Is there a way to model these covariates using 'gdistsamp'? if not, what is the next best option?

Vaughn

